On Sat, Oct 25, 2014 at 12:36 PM, John Cowan <cowan@mercury.ccil.org> wrote=
:

> Jorge Llamb=C3=ADas scripsit:
>
> > artmxozaiko
> > kaktnxo
> > mastlxa
>
> etc. etc.
>
> These words are far worse than their x-less equivalents.  Better to
> reformulate
> the grammar to allow art-mo-zai-ko.


I see that as a feature, not a problem. The syllable "-art-" may look fine
to English speakers, but it's unlojbanic, lojban only allows single
consonant codas. "ar,tm,xo,zai,ko" is horrible, of course, consonantal
syllables should be avoided. Why not better make it "larmozaiko"?

mu'o mi'e xorxes

